  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Asrc Federal Facilities Logistics obligated $514M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Asrc Federal Facilities Logistics recorded 217,597 awards with an average award size of $2.4K. Obligations fell 31.8% year over year. Fiscal totals show a rise from $549M in FY21 to a peak near $753M in FY25, then a decline to $514M in FY26. Other Warehousing and Storage is the largest market for Asrc Federal Facilities Logistics in FY2026 to date at $172M. Petroleum Lubricating Oil and Grease Manufacturing is the second-largest market at $118M, followed by Adhesive Manufacturing at $61.2M. Electrical Apparatus and Equipment, Wiring Supplies, and Related Equipment Merchant Wholesalers account for $59.4M of obligations. The top ten NAICS markets together highlight logistics, fuels and lubricants, and industrial supplies as the dominant product and service areas for Asrc Federal Facilities Logistics this fiscal year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Asrc Federal Facilities Logistics' funding trended recently?",
        "body": "Asrc Federal Facilities Logistics' obligations rose from $549M in FY21 to $753M in FY25 before falling to $514M in FY26. Asrc Federal Facilities Logistics recorded a year-over-year decline of down 31.8% in FY2026 to date. Asrc Federal Facilities Logistics' award count and average award size in FY2026 to date are 217,597 awards and $2.4K respectively."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which markets drive Asrc Federal Facilities Logistics' FY2026 to date obligations?",
        "body": "Other Warehousing and Storage drives obligations for Asrc Federal Facilities Logistics at $172M in FY2026 to date. Petroleum Lubricating Oil and Grease Manufacturing and Adhesive Manufacturing follow at $118M and $61.2M respectively, with Electrical Apparatus and Equipment, Wiring Supplies, and Related Equipment Merchant Wholesalers at $59.4M. Asrc Federal Facilities Logistics also has obligations in All Other Miscellaneous General Purpose Machinery Manufacturing ($32M), Paint and Coating Manufacturing ($21.8M), and smaller NAICS markets listed in the top ten."
